Formless is the Higher Kind that made Old Thessia, and its true name is lost.

Old Thessia was a great world almost within the core of the [[Geography/index|Astra]], one of the first to give rise to life. In time the sphere drifted too close to the core, and the volatile magic there threatened to wipe out its people. Formless wept for them and found a way to save a scant few: through a kind of loophole in the laws of physics it gave itself up and granted its divinity to them. In doing so it gave up its name and its form. Those it saved became the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]].

When a creature so great ceases to exist in an instant, the universe rushes in to fill the space it left, and the primordial forces rebound outward with an impression of its shape. Three waves of that rebound formed links with the missing Formless: the [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragments]].
